---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n/i18n.js';

const lang = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title={t('lasea.meta.title', lang)}
  description={t('lasea.meta.description', lang)}
  ogUrl="https://kajoble.com/en/lasea"
>
  <div id="main" class="alt">
    <section id="one">
      <div class="inner">
        <header class="major">
          <h1>{t('lasea.title', lang)}</h1>
        </header>
        <span class="image main"><img src="/images/Lasea-index.jpg" alt="" /></span>
        <p><span class="image left"><img src="/images/lasea-kyla.png" alt="" /></span>During my time at LASEA, I contributed to enhancing KYLA&reg;, a central software platform used for precise control of industrial laser cutting systems. KYLA&reg; integrates CAD/CAM workflows with real-time laser execution and machine feedback to support complex operations such as cutting, engraving, drilling, and more.</p>
        <br/><br/>
        <p>In this role I:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Improved and extended the existing control software that drives laser generation and machine coordination, increasing robustness and usability.</li>
          <li>Played a key role in implementing a 3D generator component allowing users to create and preview three-dimensional machining models directly within the software.</li>
          <li>Worked closely with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless integration between the new 3D generation module, machine communication layers, and user interface components.</li>
          <li>Used C# and WPF throughout the development of performant, maintainable features in a high-precision industrial context.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This work contributed to a more capable and intuitive laser cutting suite that bridges design and actual production with powerful software tools.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="two">
      <div class="inner">
        <header class="major">
          <h2>{t('lasea.techStack', lang)}</h2>
        </header>
        <p>C#, WPF, WinForms, JSON</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
